Relevant columns and their potential usage
• lap_positions.lap_type : identify normal “Race” laps, pit‑related laps (“Pit In/Out”), and pre‑start laps (“Starting Position – Grid Drop”).  
• lap_positions.lap, lap_positions.position : position of a driver on a given lap – needed to spot position changes.  
• lap_positions.race_id, lap_positions.driver_id : primary keys to match consecutive laps belonging to the same driver and race.  
• pit_stops.race_id, pit_stops.driver_id, pit_stops.lap : laps on which a driver enters/leaves the pit – laps to be ignored because position changes are pit‑stop related.  
• retirements.race_id, retirements.driver_id, retirements.lap : laps on which a driver retires – ignore because they create artificial position changes.  
• drivers_ext.driver_id, drivers_ext.full_name : final list of full driver names.  

Typical conditions that will be useful
• lp_curr.lap_type = 'Race' AND lp_prev.lap_type = 'Race'                       – on‑track race laps only.  
• lp_curr.lap   > 1                                                              – ignore first‑lap position changes (start movements).  
• lp_curr.lap  NOT IN (SELECT lap FROM pit_stops …)                             – discard pit‑entry/exit laps.  
• lp_curr.lap  NOT IN (SELECT lap FROM retirements …)                           – discard retirement lap.  
• CASE WHEN lp_prev.position > lp_curr.position …                               – positive delta = overtakes, negative delta = was overtaken.  

Ten exploratory → final SQL queries
All queries are limited to 20 rows so you can inspect the data step by step.

```sql
-- 1. Description: See all distinct lap types that exist in lap_positions.
SELECT DISTINCT lp."lap_type"
FROM "lap_positions" AS lp
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show raw lap‑by‑lap positions for Lewis Hamilton (driver_id = 1) in the 2009 Australian GP (race_id = 1).
SELECT lp."race_id",
       lp."driver_id",
       lp."lap",
       lp."position",
       lp."lap_type"
FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp
WHERE  lp."race_id"  = 1
  AND  lp."driver_id" = 1
ORDER  BY lp."lap"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect pit‑stop laps for the same race so we know which laps to ignore.
SELECT ps."race_id",
       ps."driver_id",
       ps."lap",
       ps."stop",
       ps."duration"
FROM   "pit_stops" AS ps
WHERE  ps."race_id" = 1
ORDER  BY ps."driver_id", ps."lap"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Check retirements to know which laps introduce non‑overtake position changes.
SELECT r."race_id",
       r."driver_id",
       r."lap",
       r."retirement_type"
FROM   "retirements" AS r
WHERE  r."race_id" = 18    -- example race
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: For Hamilton in race 1, show consecutive‑lap deltas (ignoring lap 1).
SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
       lp_curr."driver_id",
       lp_curr."lap",
       lp_prev."position" AS "pos_lap_minus_1",
       lp_curr."position" AS "pos_lap",
       (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") AS "delta"
FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
       ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
      AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
      AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
WHERE  lp_curr."race_id"   = 1
  AND  lp_curr."driver_id" = 1
  AND  lp_curr."lap"      > 1
  AND  lp_curr."lap_type"  = 'Race'
  AND  lp_prev."lap_type"  = 'Race'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate Hamilton’s overtakes vs times he was overtaken across ALL races.
WITH deltas AS (
  SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
         lp_curr."driver_id",
         CASE
           WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") > 0
             THEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position")      -- he overtook others
           ELSE 0
         END AS overtakes,
         CASE
           WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") < 0
             THEN (lp_curr."position" - lp_prev."position")      -- he was overtaken
           ELSE 0
         END AS was_overtaken
  FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
  JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
         ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
        AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
        AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
  WHERE  lp_curr."lap"       > 1
    AND  lp_curr."lap_type"   = 'Race'
    AND  lp_prev."lap_type"   = 'Race'
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (
          SELECT ps."lap" FROM "pit_stops" ps
          WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
            AND ps."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
    AND  lp_prev."lap" NOT IN (
          SELECT ps."lap" FROM "pit_stops" ps
          WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_prev."race_id"
            AND ps."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id")
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (
          SELECT r."lap" FROM "retirements" r
          WHERE r."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
            AND r."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
)
SELECT d."driver_id",
       SUM(d.overtakes)     AS total_overtakes,
       SUM(d.was_overtaken) AS total_times_overtaken
FROM   deltas AS d
WHERE  d."driver_id" = 1
GROUP  BY d."driver_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Same aggregation as #6 but for every driver in one example race (race_id = 18).
WITH deltas AS (
  SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
         lp_curr."driver_id",
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") > 0
              THEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") ELSE 0 END AS overtakes,
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") < 0
              THEN (lp_curr."position" - lp_prev."position") ELSE 0 END AS was_overtaken
  FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
  JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
         ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
        AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
        AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
  WHERE  lp_curr."race_id" = 18
    AND  lp_curr."lap"    > 1
    AND  lp_curr."lap_type" = 'Race'
    AND  lp_prev."lap_type" = 'Race'
)
SELECT d."driver_id",
       SUM(d.overtakes)     AS overtakes,
       SUM(d.was_overtaken) AS times_overtaken
FROM   deltas AS d
GROUP  BY d."driver_id"
ORDER  BY times_overtaken DESC, overtakes ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate overtakes / times‑overtaken ACROSS ALL races for EVERY driver.
WITH deltas AS (
  SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
         lp_curr."driver_id",
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") > 0
              THEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") ELSE 0 END AS overtakes,
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") < 0
              THEN (lp_curr."position" - lp_prev."position") ELSE 0 END AS was_overtaken
  FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
  JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
         ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
        AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
        AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
  WHERE  lp_curr."lap"     > 1
    AND  lp_curr."lap_type" = 'Race'
    AND  lp_prev."lap_type" = 'Race'
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
    AND  lp_prev."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_prev."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id")
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT r."lap"
                               FROM "retirements" r
                               WHERE r."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND r."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
)
SELECT d."driver_id",
       SUM(d.overtakes)     AS total_overtakes,
       SUM(d.was_overtaken) AS total_times_overtaken
FROM   deltas AS d
GROUP  BY d."driver_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Return driver_ids where they are overtaken more than they overtake.
WITH deltas AS (
  SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
         lp_curr."driver_id",
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") > 0
              THEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") ELSE 0 END AS overtakes,
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") < 0
              THEN (lp_curr."position" - lp_prev."position") ELSE 0 END AS was_overtaken
  FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
  JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
         ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
        AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
        AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
  WHERE  lp_curr."lap"     > 1
    AND  lp_curr."lap_type" = 'Race'
    AND  lp_prev."lap_type" = 'Race'
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
    AND  lp_prev."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_prev."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id")
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT r."lap"
                               FROM "retirements" r
                               WHERE r."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND r."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
)
SELECT d."driver_id"
FROM   deltas AS d
GROUP  BY d."driver_id"
HAVING SUM(d.was_overtaken) > SUM(d.overtakes)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – list the full names of those drivers who have been overtaken more than they overtake (all the exclusions applied).
WITH deltas AS (
  SELECT lp_curr."race_id",
         lp_curr."driver_id",
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") > 0
              THEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") ELSE 0 END AS overtakes,
         CASE WHEN (lp_prev."position" - lp_curr."position") < 0
              THEN (lp_curr."position" - lp_prev."position") ELSE 0 END AS was_overtaken
  FROM   "lap_positions" AS lp_curr
  JOIN   "lap_positions" AS lp_prev
         ON lp_curr."race_id"   = lp_prev."race_id"
        AND lp_curr."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id"
        AND lp_curr."lap"       = lp_prev."lap" + 1
  WHERE  lp_curr."lap"     > 1                -- ignore start‑lap
    AND  lp_curr."lap_type" = 'Race'          -- on‑track laps
    AND  lp_prev."lap_type" = 'Race'
    -- ignore this lap & previous lap if the driver is in the pit
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
    AND  lp_prev."lap" NOT IN (SELECT ps."lap"
                               FROM "pit_stops" ps
                               WHERE ps."race_id" = lp_prev."race_id"
                                 AND ps."driver_id" = lp_prev."driver_id")
    -- ignore if driver retires on this lap
    AND  lp_curr."lap" NOT IN (SELECT r."lap"
                               FROM "retirements" r
                               WHERE r."race_id" = lp_curr."race_id"
                                 AND r."driver_id" = lp_curr."driver_id")
)
, tot AS (
  SELECT d."driver_id",
         SUM(d.overtakes)     AS total_overtakes,
         SUM(d.was_overtaken) AS total_times_overtaken
  FROM   deltas AS d
  GROUP  BY d."driver_id"
)
SELECT de."full_name"
FROM   tot
JOIN   "drivers_ext" AS de
       ON de."driver_id" = tot."driver_id"
WHERE  tot.total_times_overtaken > tot.total_overtakes
ORDER  BY tot.total_times_overtaken - tot.total_overtakes DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

You can run the final query (#10) to obtain the complete list of drivers whose on‑track “times‑overtaken” count exceeds their on‑track overtakes, after filtering out pit‑stop, retirement, and first‑lap position changes.
